<title>BELGIUM: Belgian tax receipts up 5.5 pct in first five mths.</title>
<headline>Belgian tax receipts up 5.5 pct in first five mths.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total Belgian fiscal receipts were up 9.1 percent in May from May 1996 and up 5.5 percent in the first five months of 1997 from the same 1996 period, the Finance Ministry said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>TAX RECEIPTS (in million bfr)</p>
<p>				     MAY 97	 MAY 96     pct change</p>
<p>    Total			  160,720	147,376	9.1</p>
<p>    Direct taxation	    104,630	 55,918     87.1</p>
<p>    V.A.T and similar taxes   45,071	 39,218     14.9</p>
<p>CUMULATIVE TAX RECEIPTS (in million bfr)</p>
<p>				     JAN-MAY 97   JAN-MAY 96 pct change</p>
<p>    Total			    961,166	911,146    5.5</p>
<p>    Direct taxation		571,662	513,901   11.2</p>
<p>    V.A.T and similar taxes    238,081	228,194    4.3</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
